  This article discusses various aspects of typesetting the author's book
  \titleref{Form \textit{\&} Number: A History of Mathematical Beauty} and some
  of the techniques that were adopted and which have, in certain cases, formed
  the bases of new packages. Topics discussed include: the creation of two-page
  spreads showing tilings for part divisions; notes and other content in the
  margins; ensuring consistency in graphics; font modifications that were
  necessary because of unforeseen combinations involving accented letters;
  indexing; running heads; the build process.
